Yet on his fear’s sense keepeth still the load
Of that brink-nothing he doth but suspect;
And the cold terror moves to him more near

note:
I will not quiver in the frailest bone,
You will not note a flicker of defeat;
My heart shall tremble not its fate to meet,

notched:
but it is not a question--just a call--;
Show me then, only your notched inches climbing up the garden wall,
I like you best when you were small.

Missing the turn still, baffled by the door;
Smooth endless days, notched here and there with knives;
A weary, wormy darkness, spurred i’ the flank

notch:
An imitative dint that seemed my own;
This notch, not of my doing,
Misled me to my ruin.
